# Stone Removal Game

**LeetCode Problem:** [Stone Removal Game](https://leetcode.com/problems/stone-removal-game/)

## Approach: Simulation

- Alice starts the game and initially needs to remove 10 stones.
- After every turn, the required number of stones decreases by 1.
- Each player removes the minimum of the required stones and the remaining stones.
- If the remaining stones are fewer than the required number, the current player cannot make a valid move, and the other player wins.
- Alternate turns between Alice and Bob until one player cannot make a move.

## Code

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    bool canAliceWin(int n) {
        bool Alice = true;
        int pivot = 10;

        while(true) {
            if(n < pivot) return !Alice;

            int mini = min(pivot, n);
            n = n - mini;

            if(Alice) Alice = false;
            else Alice = true;

            pivot--;
        }

        return true;
    }
};
```

## Complexity Analysis

- **Time Complexity:** O(1) — At most 10 iterations are performed.
- **Space Complexity:** O(1) — Only a constant amount of extra space is used.

## Key Learning

This problem can be solved using simple simulation by tracking the number of remaining stones, the required stones per turn, and the current player.
